      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "nesarc_data['CHECK321'] = nesarc_data['CHECK321'].replace(' ', np.nan)\n",
        "\n",
        "nesarc_data['TAB12MDX'] = pd.to_numeric(nesarc_data['TAB12MDX'], errors='coerce')\n",
        "nesarc_data['CHECK321'] = pd.to_numeric(nesarc_data['CHECK321'], errors='coerce')\n",
        "nesarc_data['S3AQ3C1'] = pd.to_numeric(nesarc_data['S3AQ3C1'], errors='coerce')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "4db959b6",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Part 2: Row Selection and Data Subsetting\n",
        "\n",
        "In Lab 1 frequency distributions were calculated on the entire dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "We will now focus on a subset:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Age between 18 and 25 inclusive\n",
        "- Smoked within the last 12 months (CHECK321 = 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "This produces a dataset tailored to the research question."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "a753b891",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Population vs Analytical Sample\n",
        "The original NESARC dataset contains the full population of respondents. Analysts often create a smaller analytical sample that is relevant to a research question. In this lab we focus on smokers aged 18–25.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "0448d06e",
      "metadata": {
        "vscode": {
          "languageId": "plaintext"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "## Logical Operators\n",
        "\n",
        "== equal to\n",
        "!= not equal to\n",
        "> greater than\n",
        "< less than\n",
        ">= greater than or equal to\n",
        "<= less than or equal to\n",
        "& AND\n",
        "| OR\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "d9d969fc",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Example logical expressions\n",
        "# age >= 18\n",
        "# age <= 25\n",
        "# CHECK321 == 1\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5e560ed3",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Creating Copies of DataFrames\n",
        "A copy allows experimentation without changing the original dataframe.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "922ce56f",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "subset2 = nesarc_data.copy()\n",
        "print('Rows in subset2:', len(subset2))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "e7fa63b7",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Using loc\n",
        "loc allows row and column selection and updating based on conditions.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "c890e17d",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Simple loc example\n",
        "# students.loc[students['Age'] > 20]\n"
      ]
