    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "130bce6b",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Part 3: Missing Data Management\n",
        "\n",
        "A common task in analytics is deciding how to treat unknown or invalid values.\n",
        "\n",
        "For variable S3AQ3B1:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Values 1–8 are valid categories.\n",
        "- Value 9 means unknown.\n",
        "\n",
        "Unknown values do not help answer the research question and should be converted to missing values (NaN)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "5248687a",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "nesarc_data['S3AQ3B1'].dtype"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "ac9903db",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "nesarc_data['S3AQ3B1'] = pd.to_numeric(nesarc_data['S3AQ3B1'])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "17fc4200",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print('Counts for S3AQ3B1')\n",
        "print(nesarc_data['S3AQ3B1'].value_counts(sort=True))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "437ea50c",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## What is NaN?\n",
        "NaN means Not a Number and is used by pandas to represent missing values. In the next line of code we replace any NaN's with the number 9."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "fce4aca5",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "nesarc_data['S3AQ3B1'].replace(to_replace=9, value=np.nan, inplace=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "68a2e32d",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print((nesarc_data['S3AQ3B1'] == 9).sum())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "d506e5dd",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(nesarc_data['S3AQ3B1'].isnull().sum())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "6ba54623",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "exercise"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Exercise\n",
        "# Re-run the frequency distribution for S3AQ3B1\n",
        "# and verify that 9 no longer appears."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "316ceca5",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Part 4: Recovering Meaningful Missing Data\n",
        "\n",
        "Survey datasets frequently contain skip patterns.\n",
        "\n",
        "Example:\n",
        "\n",
        "If a person did not drink alcohol in the last 12 months,\n",
        "there is no reason to ask how often they drank.\n",
        "\n",
        "In these situations, blank values may actually contain useful information."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cbfe3384",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print('count of nulls')\n",
        "print((nesarc_data['S2AQ8A'].isnull()).sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "print('count of empty strings')\n",
        "print((nesarc_data['S2AQ8A'] == '').sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "print('count of spaces')\n",
        "print((nesarc_data['S2AQ8A'] == ' ').sum())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "7ebc2da9",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "nesarc_data['S2AQ8A'] = nesarc_data['S2AQ8A'].replace(' ', np.nan)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "a6535d6a",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print('Counts for S2AQ8A')\n",
        "print(nesarc_data['S2AQ8A'].value_counts(sort=True, dropna=False))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "26ce2018",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "example"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "nesarc_data.loc[\n",
        "    (nesarc_data['S2AQ3'] != 9) &\n",
        "    (nesarc_data['S2AQ8A'].isnull()),\n",
        "    'S2AQ8A'\n",
        "] = 11"
      ]
    },
